# Gray-flow User-Agent identity suffix

**When to apply:** ONLY for **slot-machine themed** games. Known slot themes:
**Joker, Egypt, Zeus, Magma / Lava**. For any non-slot theme (runners,
clickers without a slot wrapper, arcade, puzzle, etc.) do NOT add the suffix.

**If you are not sure whether the game is a slot theme, STOP and ASK the
user before adding the suffix.** Do not guess.

When the game IS a slot theme, append the app identity after the standard
browser User-Agent, space-separated:

```
<browser UA> appid/<bundleId> appname/<AppName>
```

- `appid/`   → the application id / bundle id (e.g. `com.super.game`)
- `appname/` → a space-free app name token in PascalCase (e.g. `GameNaming`)

Example (full):

```
Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 15; SM-S931U Build/AP3A.240905.015.A2) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/132.0.6834.163 Mobile Safari/537.36 appid/com.super.game appname/GameNaming
```

Rules:
- The same augmented UA must be used by BOTH the HTTP client and the WebView
  (`setUserAgent`), so traffic stays consistent.
- `appname` must contain no spaces (use PascalCase).
- Keep the suffix as the very last segment, after `Mobile Safari/537.36`.
- Source the values from the central config / facade — never hardcode at the
  call site.
